213 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (Reframing narcotics policy requires delegates to reject false binaries. The choice is not between being soft on drugs and being indifferent to human suffering, nor between public health and public safety. A credible policy can recognize addiction as a medical condition while still treating organized trafficking as serious crime. It can protect communities without criminalizing illness. It can uphold the drug control conventions while respecting the ICCPR, due process and the right to health. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
214 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (The central finding of this paper is that drug policy becomes more legitimate when it distinguishes people, behaviours and harms. Personal use and dependence require health-led responses. Low-level, coerced or survival-based offending requires proportionate sanctions and )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
